*  ============================================================================
*  PB-1s PER-SITE SNAPSHOT CELL -- root cause verified s107 (Claude Opus 5).
*  A pattern-valued statement that needs an MKPAT blob (an ALT is enough) has
*  every plain variable reference snapshotted into a hidden global named per
*  LOWERING SITE: "PAT$<blob>$V<i>" (lower_snobol4.c:2222 and :2504, "%s$V%d").
*  The built pattern DEFER-reads that global BY NAME at match time.
*  Manual p.85-86: each construction freezes ITS OWN values at construction
*  time ("NPAT captures the value of variable N at the time of pattern
*  construction"); only unary * defers.  One cell per SITE cannot do that.
*  Oracle: /home/claude/x64/bin/sbl -b <file>
*  ============================================================================
*  RED -- SILENT WRONG ANSWER, exit 0, both modes (m3 == m4).  NOT self-referential,
*  so no cycle and no crash: iteration 1 freezes c='a' into a pattern kept in SAVED,
*  then iteration 2 overwrites the SAME per-site cell with c='b'.  SAVED must still
*  match 'a' (manual p.85-86).  SCRIP prints NOMATCH -- worse than the crash because
*  it is silent.  This defect was MASKED: the cycle crashed such programs first.
        c = 'a'
        n = 0
LP      n = n + 1
        p = ('X' | c)
        saved = IDENT(n,1) p
        c = 'b'
        LT(n,2)                         :S(LP)
        'a' saved                       :F(NO)
        OUTPUT = 'MATCHED stale'        :(FIN)
NO      OUTPUT = 'NOMATCH stale'
FIN
END
